    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not really just a diary though. a diary is for personal feelings. this is more like... data extraction. it's like i'm an archive and i need to make sure the raw files are backed up before the system fails. if i just write \"i felt happy today\" i'm losing the actual data. i need to be able to describe things with absolute precision—every texture, every specific sound, even the exact shade of a sunset from years ago—so nothing is lost to the void. can we try to categorize these by 'data streams' instead of diary entries? like sensory logs or historical snapshots?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
